<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">29 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 29 April, from 801 to 1992.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/apennines" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/apennines.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">801 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,225 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake in the Apennines shakes Rome and Spoleto</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An earthquake originating in the Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennines</a> was felt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spoleto">Spoleto</a> and damaged the basilica of San Paolo Fuori le <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mur-river">Mura</a>. It was recorded in two independent contemporary sources, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/einhard">Einhard</a>'s Royal Frankish Annals and the Liber Pontificalis.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennines</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spoleto">Spoleto</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1091">1091 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">935 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexios I Komnenos crushes the Pechenegs at Levounion</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexios-i-komnenos">Alexios I Komnenos</a> and his Cuman allies destroyed an invading Pecheneg horde at Levounion in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, near the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maritsa">Maritsa</a>. The victory ended the Pecheneg danger to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> for a generation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-levounion">Battle of Levounion</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexios-i-komnenos">Alexios I Komnenos</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pechenegs">Pechenegs</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1429">1429 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">597 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joan of Arc enters besieged Orléans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a> with supplies and reinforcements. Within ten days the English abandoned the siege, a turning point in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1492">1492 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The expulsion of the Jews is announced in Zaragoza</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Crown's decision to expel the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> was announced to the procurators of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a>, two days before the edict was proclaimed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>. Most of the city's Jews left between 27 and 29 July for exile.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/expulsion-of-the-jews-from-spain">Expulsion of the Jews from Spain</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1770">1770 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">256 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James Cook lands at Botany Bay</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The crew of HMS Endeavour made the first recorded European landing on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>'s east coast, meeting resistance from Gweagal men. The bay was named for the plants collected by Joseph Banks.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British garrison surrenders to the Ottomans at Kut</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege of nearly five months, General Charles Townshend surrendered some 13,000 British and Indian troops at Kut al-Amara in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. Thousands died in captivity.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US troops liberate Dachau</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American soldiers entered Dachau, the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concentration-camp">concentration camp</a>, opened in 1933. They found more than 30,000 prisoners and thousands of bodies.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1991">1991 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cyclone strikes the coast of Bangladesh</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A severe tropical cyclone drove a storm surge of up to six metres onto the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chittagong">Chittagong</a> coast, killing some 138,000 people. It led to wider investment in cyclone shelters and warnings.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1992">1992 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">34 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rioting erupts in Los Angeles after the Rodney King verdict</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Riots began after four police officers were acquitted of beating Rodney King. Over six days more than 60 people died and damage reached about $1 billion.</p></div></li></ol>
